<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Slotline — booking pages that get timezones right' }) %>
<%- include('partials/nav', { active: '' }) %>

<main class="wrap narrow">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Share your availability. <span class="gradient-text">Let people book it.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      You set your hours once, in your own timezone. Visitors see them in theirs.
      Everything is stored as an instant in UTC, so nothing shifts when the clocks do —
      and two people cannot take the same slot, however close together they click.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <form method="post" action="/demo-login">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Open the demo account →</button>
      </form>
      <% if (demoHost) { %>
        <a class="btn" href="/<%= demoHost.slug %>">See the public booking page</a>
      <% } %>
    </div>
    <div class="chips">
      <span class="chip">DST-correct slots</span>
      <span class="chip">Calendar invites</span>
      <span class="chip">No double bookings</span>
      <span class="chip">No signup to try</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hint" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      The demo account is already set up: weekly hours, two meeting types and a few
      bookings. It signs you in as <code><%= demoEmail %></code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-label">What is actually hard here</p>
    <h2>“Tuesday at 09:00” is not a fixed moment.</h2>
    <div class="split" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">◷</div>
        <h3>Wall time, not offsets</h3>
        <p>Availability is converted per day through the host's zone, so 09:00 stays 09:00 after the clocks change instead of drifting an hour.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">⊘</div>
        <h3>Times that do not exist</h3>
        <p>New York has no 02:30 on 8 March. A round-trip check drops those slots rather than quietly offering a meeting at an hour that never happens.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">⇄</div>
        <h3>Rendered in your zone</h3>
        <p>A visitor in Tokyo books a New York host and sees a different date — same instant, both correct.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">🔒</div>
        <h3>The database says no</h3>
        <p>An exclusion constraint makes an overlapping booking impossible to store, so the loser of a race gets a clear message instead of a clash.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <a href="https://github.com/0211IkeVenLouie/slotline#the-hard-part">Read the full write-up →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Have an account?</h2>
    <p><a href="/login">Sign in</a> · <a href="/signup">Create one</a></p>
  </section>
</main>
<footer class="site wrap"><span class="faint">Slotline · Node, Postgres, Resend</span></footer>
</body></html>
